  "body": "M12.1 stage 2 of the Solidcore retirement gate. Stage 1 (68efb11) put solidcore 1.0.1 (tangency-labs' Apache-2.0 pure-Rust port of NVIDIA's SMLib) behind a `Kernel` seam in `camcraft-kernel`, with truck as the reference impl, and benched subtract and offset. This PR adds **union, intersection and edge blends (round/chamfer)** to the seam and the bench. **No production path is switched**: nothing outside `camcraft-kernel` depends on it.\n\n## What changed\n- `Kernel` trait: `boolean_union`, `boolean_intersect`, `blend_edges(solid, picks, radius, Blend::Round | Chamfer)`. truck implements union/intersect through truck-shapeops `or`/`and`. Its `blend_edges` returns `Unsupported` (truck has no fillet), and a test asserts that.\n- `src/solidcore_blend.rs` (new): picks resolve to edges (256 samples plus golden-section refinement, `PICK_TOL` 1e-3). A pick on two edges at once (a vertex, or a point on a cylinder's seam) is refused as ambiguous. Then the port's `fillet_edges`, followed by a result law: a manifold solid, inside the source box, whose volume actually moved.\n- Seam guards: face-less boolean operands are refused (the port returns the **whole box** for `box & empty`, now pinned). The blend radius guard is conservative on purpose (decision 4).\n- `tests/common/mod.rs` holds the shared `Want`/`verdict`. Stage 1's 8 tests are all kept, and the count goes to 16.\n\n## Agreement numbers (debug, default tolerances: truck mesh 1e-3 + boolean 1e-2)\n| fixture | solidcore abs. error vs closed form | truck abs. error | cross gap (default) | cross gap (heavy lane, 10x finer) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| box-union-box-corner (1875) | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| box-union-cylinder-boss (1000+20π) | 2.6e-9 | 1.7e-2 | 1.7e-2 | 2.9e-3 |\n| box-intersect-box-corner (125) | 2.8e-14 | 0 | 2.8e-14 | 2.8e-14 |\n| box-intersect-cylinder (40π) | 7.6e-9 | 3.4e-2 | 3.4e-2 | 5.7e-3 |\n| (stage 1) cylinder-through-box / blind-pocket | 2.8e-8 / 4.2e-8 | 3.4e-2 / 2.6e-2 | same | 5.7e-3 / 2.8e-3 |\n\nAll bounding boxes agree within 1.5e-5 (truck's chord), and solidcore's within 1e-14.\n\nBlends (solidcore only, checked against closed forms at 1e-6 relative; **truck: not yet - no blend in truck**):\n| fixture | abs. error |\n|---|---|\n| cube round 1 / 4 / all 12 edges r2 (12 = Steiner, spherical corners) | 4.7e-8 / 9.0e-9 / 4.7e-7 |\n| cube chamfer 1 / 4 / all 12 edges d2 (12 = inclusion-exclusion + bevel tetrahedra) | 1e-13 / 2e-13 / 1e-13 |\n| L-block concave round r2 / chamfer d2 (material added) | 1.2e-9 / 4.5e-13 |\n| cylinder top rim / both rims round r1 (Pappus) | 3.1e-6 / 2.2e-6 |\n| hole rim round r1 on a boolean result (Pappus) | 4.4e-7 |\n| **NOT YET** cylinder rim chamfer d1, port default path | 5.3e-4 (1.9e-6 rel - fails), upstream WR-421; pinned as a finding |\n| same with opt-in `fillet_chamfer_cone_on_arc` | 1.1e-5 (4e-8 rel) - passes |\n\n## Port findings (pinned in `KNOWN_PORT_VERDICTS_STAGE2`)\n- `box & empty` -> `Ok solid V=1000` (a wrong answer that looks like a valid solid). The seam refuses empty operands.\n- `box & disjoint box` -> `Ok non-solid`. The seam's result check turns it into `Err`.\n- `fillet r NaN` -> `Err`. `fillet r6 on a 10-cube edge` -> correct (922.743), but the seam still refuses it (conservative guard).\n- solidcore never panicked on any degenerate input.\n\n## Gate\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel`: agreement 2 + 2 ignored, blend 6, corrupt_input 6, all green\n- `cargo test --release -p camcraft-kernel -- --ignored` (heavy lane): green\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n- `cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p camcraft-kernel`: passes\n\nPinning tests: `boolean_fixtures_agree_across_kernels`, `boolean_fixtures_agree_at_fine_tessellation`, `cube_blends_match_closed_form`, `concave_l_blends_match_closed_form`, `rim_rounds_match_pappus`, `not_yet_rim_chamfer_default_path_stays_a_finding`, `rim_chamfer_agrees_with_cone_on_arc_fix`, `truck_offers_no_edge_blend`, `seam_refuses_degenerate_blends_and_empty_booleans`, `port_stage2_degenerates_never_panic_and_match_pinned_verdicts`.\n\n## Still owed before truck's kernel role retires (#27 stays open)\n- A corrupt-input corpus through a solidcore importer. None exists, and STEP stays on truck-stepio.\n- M4.2's wasm CI job taking `camcraft-kernel` (the local check passes).\n- Healing benched.\n- The first production consumer (boolean stock ops, or face/island recognition) switched behind this bench.\n- Upstream reports for the pinned port findings.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/27-solidcore-bench.md`.\n\nChangelog: kernel seam (M12.1 stage 2) - boolean union/intersection and edge rounds/chamfers through solidcore, benched against truck and closed forms; no production path switched yet\n\nRefs #27\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
